  "aiContextParagraph": "President Prabowo Subianto has publicly addressed the necessity of finding a successor for the vice presidential role, emphasizing that the selection process will commence immediately following his return from international diplomatic engagements in Manila and Shenzhen. The move has prompted widespread discussion within Indonesian political circles, with various parties reacting to the vacancy. Notably, the Golkar party has identified a list of eight potential figures deemed suitable for the office. Conversely, other political entities, such as the PKS, have chosen to abstain from proposing specific candidates, expressing that the final decision rests solely with the president. The discourse surrounding the potential transition has involved speculation regarding prominent public figures and officials, though the president has maintained that the selection will involve careful consideration of external guidance. The national assembly has also begun internal discussions regarding the procedural requirements for filling the vacancy.",
